    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n46337" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">suc-cŭtĭo</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">subc-</span></b> ), ussi, ussum,
		3, v. a.
		sub-quatio, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to fling up from below</i>, <i>fling
				aloft</i>, <i>toss up</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">orbes rotarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lucr.
					6, 551</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">currus alte,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					2, 166</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mare,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Q. N. 5, 1, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vasculum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 2, p. 166</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caput,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Mag. p. 333</span></i>
			 et saep.—* </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vultūs succussus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Val.
					Max. 6, 9</span></i>
			 ext. 5.</div>
